well brian shows on the las vegas strip  are dark  and the performers and the entertainers  are certainly suffering  tonight many of them gathered on the las  vegas strip to send a  unique message to lawmakers eight news  now reporter joe moeller was there and  he joins us now live with more on their  message  joe las vegas is known as the  entertainment capital when the  entertainment industry provides  thousands of jobs here in the valley  well this evening hundreds of  demonstrators came out here to the strip  to shed light on how badly the industry  is being impacted  [Music]  from the live music to shows on water  las vegas is  entertainment entertainment is the  lifeblood of this town millions come  here to be  entertained as the pandemic continues  thousands in the entertainment industry  remain without work  we have no idea when we're ever going to  go back to work  a summer heat wave did not stop hundreds  from the industry from taking to the  strip  for a rally wednesday we've been out of  work for well over  six months from wardrobe attendance to  stagehands people from all parts of the  industry  say they want more done by lawmakers to  come up with a plan to get the industry  back up and running  if governor sysolak states that we can  open our theaters we don't just reopen  the next day  it's not that simple we need audience  members we need people to fly to las  vegas we need people for hotel rooms  we need any number of things to get our  business back in place  we need the aid organizer david shulman  says he wants people to know how bad the  pandemic is  impacting them and for people to know  how big the industry is for the area  we can say that there are 68 thousand  entertainment workers out of work here  in the city of las vegas  that's approximately 2.8 million but  until people see our numbers  they don't really understand what that  means demonstrators say not only are  they without work  but many are still without unemployment  benefits it makes me sad it's upsetting  it's hurting i've tried to help as many  friends and even family members as i can  try to get through to unemployment  organizers say yet another demonstration  is planned for september first and on  that evening of that demonstration  buildings across the valley will  turn their lights red to stand in  solidarity with the entertainment  industry and the workers in it  reporting live here on the las vegas  strip i'm john muller 8 news now
 

